  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Initial release: optional SkiaSharp image helpers for JRK.JevRunner.\n\nImage scaling\n- ImageScaler.Upscale and Downscale scale proportionally using the shorter and longer side, respectively, with custom bounds (280 and 1568 by default).\n- Scaling returns PNG bytes without modifying the source. Results still outside other API limits are not rejected.\n\nImage validation\n- ImageValidator inspects actual PNG/JPEG contents and checks inclusive 280-1568-pixel width and height and the 16 MiB file limit.\n- Rejects animated PNG and non-default EXIF orientation. Checks pixel decoding when other checks pass.\n- ImageValidationResult exposes typed dimension or string errors, SuggestedScaling, and ThrowIfInvalid(). Errors provide GetErrorMessage(); ImageDimensionError.GetErrors() checks custom dimension bounds.\n- SuggestedScaling groups dimension violations by direction. It ignores other errors and does not guarantee valid resized output.\n\nExperimental automatic adjustment\n- AddImageAssetWithAutoAdjustment validates, attempts one suggested resize, and registers the result without changing source files.\n- Unchanged files retain their detected format and bytes; resized images become PNG.\n- Validation, byte loading, and resizing consistently use the supplied file system.\n- Adjusted output is not revalidated. Request-wide limits require separate validation.\n\nBounding-box rendering\n- BoxRenderer.DrawBox accepts a single BoxAnswer or an enumerable through the AppliedBox union.\n- Draws normalized bounding-box outlines with shared configurable color and stroke width.\n\nPlatform and file-system support\n- Renderer, validator, and scaler support injectable file access through TruePath and IFileSystem.\n- Includes Linux native assets alongside SkiaSharp's Windows and macOS assets.\n- Targets .NET 11 and uses preview C# union support.",
